{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774026710,"nonce":"Xk/rNA+4afHf+Glazn8hZcbvjHw=","message":"**Round 2 synthesis — liveness, assignment, activity monitor**\n\nTwo independent analyses (Opus + Gemini) converged on:\n\n**Liveness is an overlay, not a state.** Derived at query time: work unit → sessions on that branch → checkLiveness(). Three tiers: SDK (precise, processing flag), PTY (PID alive), external (JSONL mtime). No \"working\" state in the issue state machine.\n\n**Assignment is sticky with staleness flagging.** Worktree exists = assigned. Session dies = still assigned. Stale = flagged in UI, never auto-released. This matches how human developers work (assigned a ticket, sessions come and go).\n\n**Issue state machine stays simple**: open → committed → merged (+ abandoned). Four states total.\n\n**Activity monitor gaps**: (1) last_active never written, (2) SDK processing not exposed, (3) idle status never set, (4) discovered sessions lack issue links, (5) discovery pull-only, (6) no Gemini patterns.\n\n**Small implementation delta**: activate idle status, write last_active, expose SDK processing, periodic discovery, work-unit API joining branch + liveness + issues.","files":null}]}